  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training for Ukrainian SMEs on access to finance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to facilitate access to financial resources for Ukrainian businesses through training for business representatives.During the training, businesses will gain theoretical knowledge about the opportunities of making use of financial instruments and will develop practical skills to effectively apply for funding with the acquired knowledge.As a result of the effective implementation of the project, representatives of the business community will have a broader knowledge of access to finance opportunities, in particular for small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) for businesses, improve their soft and hard skills in attracting financing. In doing so, the overall capacity of the private sector will be enhanced.This project is a follow-up of Project PST24UA01: fact-finding study SMEs access to finance.The project has positive impact on:&#x2022;	SDG 8: Decent work and economic growth: support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation, access to markets.&#x2022;	SDG 9: Industry, innovation and infrastructure: support of business development and industrial growth.</narrative>
  </description>
